  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2412.04454",
  "abstract": "AGUVIS is a unified vision-based framework for autonomous GUI agents that directly operates on screen images, standardizes cross-platform interactions, and incorporates structured reasoning via inner monologue. This approach enables the development of a single model capable of operating across diverse GUI environments, promoting human-like interaction patterns and better generalization to novel interfaces.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Imagine a computer program that can interact with graphical user interfaces (GUIs) just like a human would. <strong>AGUVIS</strong> is a framework that makes this possible by using <strong>visual observations</strong> and <strong>structured reasoning</strong> to navigate complex interfaces. This approach eliminates the need for platform-specific textual representations, allowing for more natural and generalizable interface understanding.",
